# bench-rank.mjs fetches one candidate pool and then A/Bs rankings against it
# offline. That file is a local fixture — 100 KB of somebody else's titles and
# snippets, regenerated in half a minute with --fresh — and committing it would
# put a copy of the web in the history that nothing updates.
tests/eval/search-baselines/candidate-pool.json

# A LITERAL "%USERPROFILE%" DIRECTORY IS A BUG'S FOOTPRINT, NOT A SOURCE TREE.
#
# The agent was once handed the placeholder `%USERPROFILE%` instead of a real
# home directory (see packages/shared-types/src/external-context.js), typed it
# back into PowerShell, and PowerShell — which does not expand %VAR% — resolved
# it as a RELATIVE path. So a folder literally named `%USERPROFILE%` appeared
# inside the repository, five temp files deep, and got committed. Removed from
# tracking on 22 Aug 2026; ignored here so it cannot come back.
%USERPROFILE%/
*AppDataLocalTemp*

# Session transcripts. Large, local, and the documented way a live API key
# reached a file once already — never something to publish.
transcript.txt

